data/raw/databento/
data/raw/futures/
data/raw/ibkr/
data/fixtures/*futures*
data/fixtures/*glbx*

# temp/ is disposable by contract -- see temp/README.md. Only the README is tracked.
/temp/*
!/temp/README.md

# D361 trade export: the plain CSV is regenerated by scripts/d361_export_trades.py or gunzip; the .gz is tracked
data/d361_trades_gap_up_fade.csv

# Third-party YouTube transcripts: source material read for review, never evidence.
# Anything worth keeping is quoted into docs/youtube-lessons.md or a decision record.
# The raw transcripts are disposable and are not ours to redistribute.
docs/Youtube Transcrips/

# D377 ensemble: 136 MB of reconstructed book series, 4x the largest tracked file.
# Exactly reproducible: `uv run python scripts/run_d377_hedge.py --build --draws 500` (~10 min, deterministic seeds).
# Every number the record quotes lives in the committed data/d377_hedge.json.
data/d377_ensemble.npz

# D382 scores: 114 MB of per-cell structure scores, 400x the largest tracked .npz in data/.
# Same treatment as d377_ensemble.npz above, and the same reasons.
# Exactly reproducible: `uv run python scripts/run_d382_structure_screen.py` (fixed SEED, gated fixture e22350a).
# Its two sibling artifacts ARE tracked -- data/d382_observed.json and data/d382_nulls.json -- and
# every number D382's record quotes lives in those.
data/d382_scores.npz

# Claude Code's own worktree state for the signal-hunt-part2 branch. Machine-local tooling,
# not project content, and it points at paths that exist only on this machine.
.claude/worktrees/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Bulk data panels: dropped from the index 2026-09-15 (portfolio repack)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 115 files, 844 MB, in a repository whose source is 21k lines. D70/D24 committed
# fixtures so that CHANGING one is a visible diff rather than a silent re-fetch --
# a real property, and it is kept here by other means:
#
#   * data/data_manifest.json (tracked) carries the sha256 AND the git blob id of
#     every file matched below. A changed panel is still a visible diff; the diff
#     moves to a one-line JSON change, which is more readable than a 46 MB gzip
#     blob no reviewer opens.
#   * History is NOT rewritten, so every byte is still reachable:
#         git cat-file blob <git_blob> > <path>
#   * `python scripts/build_data_manifest.py --verify` re-hashes what is on disk.
#
# Evidence stays tracked: plain .csv (the largest under data/ is 0.6 MB), every
# .json artifact a decision record quotes, and the .meta.json / _events.json
# provenance sidecars beside each panel.
/data/**/*.csv.gz
/data/**/*.parquet
/data/**/*.npz
/data/**/*.zip

# D538 re-included the two Binance panels here as a size exception; D554 purged them from the
# index and the history on 2026-09-18, and the exception went with them. They stay on disk,
# untracked and manifested, like the other 116 panels.

# The portfolio repack plan: working scaffolding for the repack above, not part of
# the record it plans. Anything it decides lands in docs/decisions/ under its own
# number, in writing, like every other decision here.
/working/PORTFOLIO_PLAN.md
/working/REVIEW_REMEDIATION_PLAN.md

# working/ SCRATCH LEAVES THE INDEX (2026-09-28). working/README.md's own rule is that a file
# here moves on "when it stops being needed -- it does not linger", and 137 tracked files say
# that did not happen. A clone was receiving 87 one-off diagnostics, drafts, CSVs, logs and
# PNGs, which is noise in the one directory a reader is least able to interpret.
#
# THE SPLIT IS NOT "ALL OF working/", and the reason is mechanical rather than aesthetic: 31
# markdown links in tracked documents point in here -- six decision records, PICKUP.md and four
# pages under docs/research/. Dropping their targets would redden check_doc_links.py, and the
# alternative, editing six decision records to remove citations, is the one thing this
# repository does not do to a dated record. So everything cited stays, and so does the leads*/
# research corpus those pages are built on (43 documents, an argued body of work rather than
# scratch). What leaves is what nothing references.
#
# Nothing is deleted: every file stays on disk, and the history keeps every version committed
# up to here. The cost is that FUTURE edits to the untracked ones are no longer backed up by a
# push, which is the trade working/README.md's "losing in-flight work is expensive" was pointing
# at -- so finished work should now actually move to temp/ rather than sit here.
/working/*
!/working/README.md
!/working/leads/
!/working/leads2/
!/working/leads3/
!/working/leads4/
!/working/leads5/
!/working/leads6/
!/working/AUDIT-flat-id-map-exposure.md
!/working/avenue3_leveraged_etf_reset.py
!/working/avenue3_window_check.py
!/working/orb_premise_checks.py
!/working/orb_check2_diagnostics.py
!/working/orb_drift_control.py
